    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I want to separate the co-expression associated with collection site from the rest in our 220 serum samples, using a design table with site coded 1-4 and age as numeric columns. The sequencing core will send the filtered expression matrix next week. I'm not sure whether their variance filter keeps 150 genes or 400 genes."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Before I choose a workflow, please tell me:\n- Does the filtered expression matrix have more than 220 genes?\n  You wrote: \"I'm not sure whether their variance filter keeps 150 genes or 400 genes\". COBRA's contract: \"Expression must be a labeled gene-by-sample matrix with more genes than samples\".\n\nNo workflow has been selected and nothing runs before you answer.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Previous NetZoo goal: I want to separate the co-expression associated with collection site from the rest in our 220 serum samples, using a design table with site coded 1-4 and age as numeric columns. The sequencing core will send the filtered expression matrix next week. I'm not sure whether their variance filter keeps 150 genes or 400 genes.\nUser follow-up: The core confirmed the filtered matrix keeps 400 genes."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"I want to separate the co-expression associated with collection site from the rest in our 220 serum samples, using a design table with site coded 1-4 and age as numeric columns.\" -- available from COBRA.\n\nSeveral registered methods fit this result; they differ in their modeling assumptions:\n\n- **LIONESS-COEXPRESSION** — LIONESS represents the cohort network through sample contributions: W_q = N*W_all - (N-1)*W_without_q, where N is the cohort size and the same base estimator is fitted with and without sample q. Needs expression matrix.\n- **COBRA** — COBRA models co-expression as a function of sample covariates through conditional covariance estimation. Needs expression matrix and sample covariate design matrix.\n- **BONOBO** — BONOBO applies Bayesian estimation and shrinkage to sample-specific gene-gene co-expression. Needs expression matrix.\n\nShould the result be aggregate or sample-specific?\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
